}

fu f.diff_reading.inspect {
    d: "What changed inside one entity, in the details pane. The pane used to print the head source beside a metric delta list, which answers how much something moved and never what moved; this is the reading a review tool gives — markers and line numbers on both sides, unchanged stretches folded away, and side by side once the column is wide enough. An entity that arrived or left is still a diff, every line of it: rendering it as plain source is what made added and unchanged look alike. Gained and lost edges are their own list and not badges on the Relationships section below, because that section draws the head graph — a relationship that disappeared has no row there to badge, and the one change a reader of a diff most wants to be told about was the one the pane could not show. It is also the only place a swap is visible: dropping one call and adding another leaves fan_out exactly where it was, so no metric delta reports it. Add and remove colours are deliberately not theme-derived — they identify a state, and a hue that reads as gone has to keep reading that way in all four themes."
